│   └── es-ES.json
└── styles/
    ├── tokens.css                # CSS variables (the palette)
    └── tailwind.css
```

Use the `@/` import alias for `src/` (configure in `vite.config.ts` and `tsconfig.json`).

## Naming conventions

Follows `01-file-organization` strictly. Concrete examples for this project:

| Thing | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Component file | `kebab-case.tsx` | `possibility-map.tsx` |
| Component export | `PascalCase` | `export function PossibilityMap()` |
| Hook file | `use-kebab-case.ts` | `use-council-stream.ts` |
| Hook export | `useCamelCase` | `useCouncilStream` |
| Store file | `kebab-case.store.ts` | `intent-profile.store.ts` |
| Store export | `useCamelCaseStore` | `useIntentProfileStore` |
| Type file | `kebab-case.ts` | `intent-profile.ts` |
| Type export | `PascalCase` | `IntentProfile`, `Energeia` |
| Constants | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `LIVEKIT_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS` |
| Boolean variable | `is/has/should/can` prefix | `isAwakened`, `hasEnergeia` |

## Styling with Tailwind v4

Map our design tokens via `@theme` (see `20-dynamis-design-system` for the full palette):

```css
@theme {
  --color-blue: #1B5E9F;
  --color-blue-accent: #2E86DE;
  --color-blue-soft: #DCE9F7;
  --color-red: #D94A38;          /* achievement / Energeia */
  --color-red-deep: #C73E2C;
  --color-red-warm: #E8654D;
  --color-success: #2EBC8F;      /* suggestion / completion */
  --color-ink: #0B1929;
  --color-ink-2: #475569;
  --color-bg: #FAFBFD;
  --font-display: "Fraunces", Georgia, serif;
  --font-body: "Manrope", system-ui, sans-serif;
}
```

Then use semantic classes: `bg-blue`, `text-red-deep`, `font-display`. Never use Tailwind's default `blue-500`, `red-600`, `gray-700`.

## Error handling (per `03-code-structure`)

- All async functions wrapped in `try/catch` at the call site that can react to the error.
- TanStack Query handles network errors via `error` state — use it in UI.
- Never `console.log` in committed code (per `pre-commit-check` skill).

## Performance defaults

- Lazy-load route components with `React.lazy` + `Suspense`.
- Memoize expensive computations with `useMemo`, not micro-optimizations.
- SVG illustrations: inline for the Dynamis tree / constellation. External `<img>` for static assets.

## Out of scope for the POC

- Server-side rendering — we are a SPA.
- Theme switching (light/dark toggle) — fixed light theme except for The Awakening and Possibility Map screens.
- All locales beyond `en-US.json` ship later; `en-US` is source of truth (per `04-i18n-english-first`).
